# Requirement Analysis Phase

## Project: ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

### 1. Introduction

The requirement analysis phase identifies the functional and non-functional requirements of the ComicCraft application.

ComicCraft is an AI-powered comic story creation system that uses Google Gemini models to generate comic stories, characters, dialogues, and panel descriptions based on user prompts.

The purpose of this phase is to understand user needs and define the software requirements necessary to develop the application.


### 2. Functional Requirements

Functional requirements describe the main features and operations of the ComicCraft system.

| S.No. | Requirement            | Description                                                             |
| ----- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1     | User Input             | Allow users to enter a story idea or prompt.                            |
| 2     | AI Story Generation    | Generate creative comic stories using Gemini models.                    |
| 3     | Character Creation     | Generate character names, personalities, and descriptions.              |
| 4     | Genre Selection        | Allow users to select comedy, horror, fantasy, adventure, etc.          |
| 5     | Comic Panel Generation | Divide the story into multiple panels.                                  |
| 6     | Dialogue Generation    | Generate dialogues for each comic panel.                                |
| 7     | AI Image Generation    | Generate comic illustrations using a compatible image-generation model. |
| 8     | Story Editing          | Allow users to edit and regenerate story content.                       |
| 9     | Comic Preview          | Display the generated comic in a panel-based layout.                    |
| 10    | Export Comic           | Allow users to download the completed comic.                            |

### 3. Non-Functional Requirements

Non-functional requirements define the quality and performance expected from the system.

| S.No. | Requirement     | Description                                                     |
| ----- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1     | Usability       | The application should have a simple, user-friendly interface.  |
| 2     | Performance     | The system should generate content within a reasonable time.    |
| 3     | Reliability     | The application should handle errors and API failures properly. |
| 4     | Security        | Protect user data and API keys from unauthorized access.        |
| 5     | Scalability     | Support an increasing number of users.                          |
| 6     | Compatibility   | Work on commonly used web browsers and devices.                 |
| 7     | Maintainability | Allow developers to update and improve the application easily.  |

### 4. Hardware Requirements

| Component | Minimum Requirement            |
| --------- | ------------------------------ |
| Processor | Intel Core i3 or equivalent    |
| RAM       | 4 GB                           |
| Storage   | 10 GB available space          |
| Device    | Desktop, laptop, or smartphone |
| Internet  | Stable internet connection     |

### 5. Software Requirements

| Software         | Purpose                         |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Operating System | Windows, Linux, or macOS        |
| Frontend         | HTML, CSS, JavaScript           |
| Backend          | Python with Flask or FastAPI    |
| AI Model         | Google Gemini API               |
| Image Generation | Compatible image-generation API |
| Database         | SQLite or Firebase              |
| Code Editor      | Visual Studio Code              |
| Browser          | Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge |

### 6. User Requirements

The system should allow users to:

* Enter their own comic story ideas.
* Select a preferred genre and story style.
* Generate stories using AI.
* Create characters and dialogues.
* Preview and edit comic panels.
* Save or download the completed comic.

### 7. Feasibility Analysis

| Type                    | Description                                                                                          |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Technical Feasibility   | Gemini API and web technologies can support AI-based comic story generation.                         |
| Economic Feasibility    | The project can be developed using free or low-cost development tools, subject to API usage charges. |
| Operational Feasibility | The simple interface makes the system accessible to beginners.                                       |
| Schedule Feasibility    | A basic prototype can be developed in stages, beginning with story and panel generation.             |

### 8. Expected Outcome

The requirement analysis phase defines the essential features, technical needs, and quality requirements of ComicCraft.

The final system is expected to provide an easy-to-use AI comic creation platform that transforms user ideas into structured comic stories with characters, dialogues, and visual panels using Gemini models and compatible image-generation technology.

